# `$left` and `$right` only mean something in a `join` condition (DS1031).
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where $left.amount > 1
---- expected
error[DS1031]: `$left` can only be used in a `join` condition
  --> query:1:27
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where $left.amount > 1
  |                           ^^^^^ not in a `join` condition
  |
  = help: `$left.column` names a column of one side of a `join`, in `on $left.a == $right.b`; elsewhere, use the column name

query 1 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
